1
00:00:32,331 --> 00:00:34,791
[Episode 8]

2
00:00:37,478 --> 00:00:39,938
Would you say the operation was a success?

3
00:00:39,938 --> 00:00:41,523
I'd say so.

4
00:00:41,523 --> 00:00:43,692
We flushed all the drugs away as planned,

5
00:00:43,692 --> 00:00:46,987
and we even secured footage
of the drugs as evidence.

6
00:00:46,987 --> 00:00:48,906
So yeah, I guess you could call it a success.

7
00:00:48,906 --> 00:00:52,159
But where did Bulgae suddenly come from?

8
00:00:52,159 --> 00:00:54,286
Jeong Ho Myung, anything strikes you?

9
00:00:54,286 --> 00:00:57,539
The car appeared just as Bulgae showed up.

10
00:00:57,539 --> 00:00:58,832
That is definitely not a coincidence.

11
00:00:58,832 --> 00:01:02,535
They moved with precision,
aiming for something specific.

12
00:01:04,463 --> 00:01:05,714
- Ah!
- You startled me!

13
00:01:05,714 --> 00:01:07,341
That car!

14
00:01:07,341 --> 00:01:08,967
- You scared me!
- The car we saw earlier

15
00:01:08,967 --> 00:01:12,763
is that van I saw a few days ago
in front of Kim Seon Jung's house.

16
00:01:12,763 --> 00:01:14,464
Let me see.

17
00:01:15,349 --> 00:01:17,267
It is, it's the same van.

18
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,636
Hey, did you see who was in it earlier?

19
00:01:28,028 --> 00:01:30,614
Once we get the vehicle records,

20
00:01:30,614 --> 00:01:32,741
finding out who that woman is
and where Bulgae is

21
00:01:32,741 --> 00:01:33,784
will just be a matter of time.

22
00:01:33,784 --> 00:01:36,078
- Right?
- Yeah, then,

23
00:01:36,078 --> 00:01:37,496
should we come up with another plan?

24
00:01:37,496 --> 00:01:42,584
No, first, we need to wrap up
the Yoo In Goo operation.

25
00:01:42,584 --> 00:01:46,088
We've already disposed of the drugs
and secured the evidence, what else is there?

26
00:01:46,088 --> 00:01:49,299
Having a hold on Yoo In Goo's leash
doesn't mean it's over.

27
00:01:49,299 --> 00:01:51,844
Yoo In Goo and Han Kyung Wook
have a lot of connections in the prosecution.

28
00:01:51,844 --> 00:01:55,931
If we mess this up, we could end up losing
all the evidence we worked so hard to secure.

29
00:01:55,931 --> 00:01:59,017
To link Han Kyung Wook by prosecuting
Yoo In Goo, we need Prosecutor Kang.

30
00:01:59,017 --> 00:02:01,812
Starting tomorrow, you and Kang Beom Ryong

31
00:02:01,812 --> 00:02:05,149
use the CCTV Gong Bok hacked
to locate Prosecutor Kang.

32
00:02:05,149 --> 00:02:08,444
If she's still on Yeongseondo Island,
she should show up on camera at least once.

33
00:02:08,444 --> 00:02:11,321
I'll look into Yoo In Goo with Ma Gong Bok.

34
00:02:11,321 --> 00:02:13,782
Me and Beom Ryong?

35
00:02:13,782 --> 00:02:16,160
Wouldn't Gong Bok be better for CCTV work?

36
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:19,997
Yeah, CCTV is his specialty.

37
00:02:19,997 --> 00:02:22,782
- Why me?
- You...

38
00:02:23,834 --> 00:02:28,380
You pushed yourself too hard today,
didn't you?

39
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:30,331
Take it easy and rest a bit.

40
00:02:31,341 --> 00:02:33,051
What's gotten into him today?

41
00:02:33,051 --> 00:02:35,637
Even when I'm trying to be considerate,
you still...

42
00:02:35,637 --> 00:02:39,183
I just don't want to see
your legs shaking next to me. What?

43
00:02:39,183 --> 00:02:42,811
- Jeez.
- My legs are perfectly fine. I'll do it.

44
00:02:42,811 --> 00:02:44,229
Hey, I never said

45
00:02:44,229 --> 00:02:45,606
- my legs were shaking.
- Anyway, let's make sure

46
00:02:45,606 --> 00:02:47,024
we wrap up the Yoo In Goo case first.

47
00:02:47,024 --> 00:02:49,318
As for Bulgae, like you said, we've
basically got everything under control.

48
00:02:49,318 --> 00:02:51,278
- No need to rush unnecessarily, right?
- Okay.

49
00:02:51,278 --> 00:02:52,654
Come on now. Drink up.

50
00:02:52,654 --> 00:02:54,573
- Cheers.
- Oh, dear.

51
00:02:54,573 --> 00:02:56,274
Good work, everyone.

52
00:03:11,131 --> 00:03:13,967
You look worried.

53
00:03:13,967 --> 00:03:15,835
It's because of Bulgae, right?

54
00:03:17,221 --> 00:03:19,473
You really are sharp, as always.

55
00:03:19,473 --> 00:03:23,227
Hey, we finally found Bulgae after 10 years,

56
00:03:23,227 --> 00:03:25,687
and now you're saying we shouldn't rush?

57
00:03:25,687 --> 00:03:27,523
That's not like you.

58
00:03:27,523 --> 00:03:30,350
You should be raging to catch him.

59
00:03:31,151 --> 00:03:32,861
So why are you acting like this?

60
00:03:32,861 --> 00:03:34,988
What's holding you back?

61
00:03:34,988 --> 00:03:38,951
Well, I saw her earlier.

62
00:03:38,951 --> 00:03:41,745
The woman who drove off with Bulgae.

63
00:03:41,745 --> 00:03:45,290
She was the police officer
Kang Beom Ryong has a crush on.

64
00:03:45,290 --> 00:03:46,991
Seriously?

65
00:03:48,043 --> 00:03:51,964
Jeez, what kind of woman is she
to be working with a North Korean agent?

66
00:03:51,964 --> 00:03:53,966
I don't know.

67
00:03:53,966 --> 00:03:57,010
No matter how I think about it,
I can't figure it out.

68
00:03:57,010 --> 00:03:59,930
Bulgae teaming up with a police officer,

69
00:03:59,930 --> 00:04:05,018
and that same officer
visiting Kim Seon Jung's house of all places.

70
00:04:05,018 --> 00:04:07,521
We need to figure out exactly
what Bulgae and that officer are after,

71
00:04:07,521 --> 00:04:12,526
and whether they're going to
get in the way of what we're doing.

72
00:04:12,526 --> 00:04:17,772
Tomorrow, Ma Gong Bok and I
will be trailing her, just so you know.

73
00:04:22,327 --> 00:04:25,122
Mr. Beom Ryong seemed pretty attached
to that officer.

74
00:04:25,122 --> 00:04:27,749
So it's better he doesn't know.

75
00:04:27,749 --> 00:04:32,296
What good would it do to find out
the woman he likes is involved with Bulgae?

76
00:04:32,296 --> 00:04:34,715
I'll wrap things up as fast as I can
starting tomorrow,

77
00:04:34,715 --> 00:04:38,302
so until then, just keep an eye
on Kang Beom Ryong.

78
00:04:38,302 --> 00:04:40,003
Got it.

79
00:04:49,995 --> 00:04:51,520
[Jeongseok Study Residence]

80
00:04:55,694 --> 00:04:57,529
Uncle, Uncle! Are you awake?

81
00:04:57,529 --> 00:04:59,406
- How do you feel?
- Nam Il? Nam Il!

82
00:04:59,406 --> 00:05:00,699
Nam Il, are you okay?

83
00:05:00,699 --> 00:05:02,117
Are you hurt anywhere?

84
00:05:02,117 --> 00:05:04,286
Is this really the time
to be worrying about me?

85
00:05:04,286 --> 00:05:05,954
You saved me yesterday.

86
00:05:05,954 --> 00:05:09,073
Yesterday... I did?

87
00:05:11,001 --> 00:05:12,920
You don't remember again?

88
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:15,297
Uncle, you turned into the Hulk yesterday.

89
00:05:15,297 --> 00:05:19,009
I heard you even asked Prosecutor Kang
to hit you on the head.

90
00:05:19,009 --> 00:05:21,470
Yeah, it was way too dangerous for you,
so I had to.

91
00:05:21,470 --> 00:05:23,055
Uncle, are you out of your mind?

92
00:05:23,055 --> 00:05:24,832
- What if that had failed?
- If you hadn't been there,

93
00:05:24,832 --> 00:05:26,975
none of this would've happened.

94
00:05:26,975 --> 00:05:30,187
Why were you involved
in a gang drug deal? Huh?

95
00:05:30,187 --> 00:05:32,356
I was tricked into going there.

96
00:05:32,356 --> 00:05:34,483
I thought it was a one-million-won day job.

97
00:05:34,483 --> 00:05:38,895
- Aiming for that one big score again...
- This time it wasn't like that!

98
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:42,032
I just wanted to earn money,

99
00:05:42,032 --> 00:05:45,818
get our house back, and get you out of here.

100
00:05:46,453 --> 00:05:50,031
I know you're going through
unnecessary trouble because of me.

101
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:53,576
You haven't eaten, have you?

102
00:06:02,219 --> 00:06:04,930
Hello, we're heading to
Heaven Capital, right?

103
00:06:04,930 --> 00:06:06,473
No.

104
00:06:06,473 --> 00:06:08,266
Weren't we supposed to be checking
Yoo In Goo's movements?

105
00:06:08,266 --> 00:06:09,434
Plans changed.

106
00:06:09,434 --> 00:06:10,894
We're going to the police substation.

107
00:06:10,894 --> 00:06:12,771
The police substation?

108
00:06:12,771 --> 00:06:18,110
So, those so-called Masked Racers
suddenly showed up

109
00:06:18,110 --> 00:06:20,654
and just dumped all the drugs into thin air?

110
00:06:20,654 --> 00:06:23,782
And you guys lost all of them?

111
00:06:23,782 --> 00:06:26,984
Yeah, well, those weren't ordinary guys.

112
00:06:31,206 --> 00:06:33,917
Yoo In Goo, you idiot!

113
00:06:33,917 --> 00:06:36,086
He can't do a single thing right.

114
00:06:36,086 --> 00:06:38,287
Useless idiot!

115
00:06:45,762 --> 00:06:48,724
Before I get dragged into this
and bleed for it,

116
00:06:48,724 --> 00:06:50,758
I'm getting out.

117
00:06:52,352 --> 00:06:56,023
Mr. Geum, how's the rebuilding of
the Kang Sik faction I mentioned before?

118
00:06:56,023 --> 00:06:57,691
We've already recruited the lower members.

119
00:06:57,691 --> 00:07:00,527
Now, we just need to change the sign.

120
00:07:00,527 --> 00:07:04,564
Okay, good job, good job.

121
00:07:07,284 --> 00:07:11,580
But Chairman, when should we start?

122
00:07:11,580 --> 00:07:12,914
Right now.

123
00:07:12,914 --> 00:07:15,792
What? R-Right now?

124
00:07:15,792 --> 00:07:17,711
Is that possible?

125
00:07:17,711 --> 00:07:20,464
Come on, is clearing out one piece of trash
really that difficult?

126
00:07:20,464 --> 00:07:22,591
I'll take care of that trash myself.

127
00:07:22,591 --> 00:07:25,135
And Mr. Geum, look into those guys
who ruined Mr. Yoo's drug deal yesterday,

128
00:07:25,135 --> 00:07:28,555
the so-called
martial arts master or Masked Racer.

129
00:07:28,555 --> 00:07:30,182
Those guys?

130
00:07:30,182 --> 00:07:34,186
They suddenly popped up on Yeongseondo Island
and keep interfering with our work.

131
00:07:34,186 --> 00:07:36,938
We can't ignore this any longer. Who knows?

132
00:07:36,938 --> 00:07:38,368
They might interfere with my work too,

133
00:07:38,368 --> 00:07:40,692
so we should deal with them before moving on.

134
00:07:40,692 --> 00:07:43,153
Now mobilize the police

135
00:07:43,153 --> 00:07:46,948
and dig through all CCTV and dashcam footage
around Yeongseon Port.

136
00:07:46,948 --> 00:07:50,202
Ah! And do it quietly
so Mr. Yoo doesn't catch on.

137
00:07:50,202 --> 00:07:52,204
Yes, don't worry about that.

138
00:07:52,204 --> 00:07:55,782
He won't be in any state to notice right now.

139
00:08:07,302 --> 00:08:11,139
We collected as much
as we could scrape together,

140
00:08:11,139 --> 00:08:13,090
but this is all we have.

141
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,642
- Come on, come on.
- No, don't do that...

142
00:08:23,944 --> 00:08:25,153
Not today.

143
00:08:25,153 --> 00:08:26,988
I said not today!

144
00:08:26,988 --> 00:08:29,241
- Who's that?
- Well...

145
00:08:29,241 --> 00:08:32,244
He's a casino client
who came to borrow money,

146
00:08:32,244 --> 00:08:35,455
but our funds ran out,
so we're sending him back.

147
00:08:35,455 --> 00:08:38,282
Funds... ran out?

148
00:08:50,262 --> 00:08:52,347
Oh my, boss, boss!

149
00:08:52,347 --> 00:08:55,851
- Breathe, breathe...
- Boss, breathe... catch your breath...

150
00:08:55,851 --> 00:08:57,552
Boss, boss!

151
00:09:01,606 --> 00:09:04,100
- Jae Soon.
- Oh, Prosecutor.

152
00:09:05,402 --> 00:09:08,196
- Are you alright?
- Yes, yes, fine, fine.

153
00:09:08,196 --> 00:09:12,993
I'm not even hurt or anything. I heard
I messed everything up yesterday. Sorry.

154
00:09:12,993 --> 00:09:16,448
No, no, it wasn't just because of you.
Don't worry about it.

155
00:09:16,448 --> 00:09:18,081
Good grief...

156
00:09:18,081 --> 00:09:22,794
I heard we couldn't catch
those Heaven Capital guys, huh?

157
00:09:22,794 --> 00:09:25,964
So, I've been thinking.

158
00:09:25,964 --> 00:09:28,633
Since Heaven Capital also lost all the drugs,

159
00:09:28,633 --> 00:09:31,136
they won't just sit back and watch, right?

160
00:09:31,136 --> 00:09:35,140
They'll definitely try something
to make up for their mistake.

161
00:09:35,140 --> 00:09:37,601
So what if we use that gap?

162
00:09:37,601 --> 00:09:38,643
How?

163
00:09:38,643 --> 00:09:42,772
We don't have any way
to track their movements.

164
00:09:42,772 --> 00:09:45,224
There is someone who might know.

165
00:09:49,487 --> 00:09:53,575
So you want me to become a double agent?

166
00:09:53,575 --> 00:09:55,735
A double agent?

167
00:09:56,745 --> 00:09:59,956
- Have I lost my mind?
- You have two choices.

168
00:09:59,956 --> 00:10:03,960
First, you come with me
to the district prosecutor's office.

169
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,337
Aiding and abetting murder,

170
00:10:05,337 --> 00:10:08,298
destruction of evidence, and bribery...

171
00:10:08,298 --> 00:10:10,550
I'll charge you with everything I can.

172
00:10:10,550 --> 00:10:12,427
Then Sergeant Kim,

173
00:10:12,427 --> 00:10:14,971
you'll obviously lose your badge,

174
00:10:14,971 --> 00:10:16,640
and probably end up eating prison food.

175
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:18,433
About 30 years, maybe?

176
00:10:18,433 --> 00:10:21,144
Come on, Prosecutor, how can you do this?

177
00:10:21,144 --> 00:10:22,270
I'm the victim here!

178
00:10:22,270 --> 00:10:24,731
I'm seriously, seriously unfairly treated!

179
00:10:24,731 --> 00:10:27,067
Then second option.

180
00:10:27,067 --> 00:10:29,069
Return to your police substation.

181
00:10:29,069 --> 00:10:31,905
Track Heaven Capital's movements.

182
00:10:31,905 --> 00:10:33,990
And report everything to us in real time.

183
00:10:33,990 --> 00:10:38,277
Then I'll try to give you
as much leniency as possible.

184
00:10:39,329 --> 00:10:43,491
So, which of the two is better?

185
00:10:51,925 --> 00:10:57,264
So I just have to
give you information, right?

186
00:10:57,264 --> 00:10:59,099
Yeah.

187
00:10:59,099 --> 00:11:01,935
But is it really okay to let him go?

188
00:11:01,935 --> 00:11:04,938
He keeps threatening people
whenever he gets a chance.

189
00:11:04,938 --> 00:11:08,608
That's right. A guy who betrays
his organization once will do it again.

190
00:11:08,608 --> 00:11:10,694
No.

191
00:11:10,694 --> 00:11:13,697
I'll keep an eye on him.

192
00:11:13,697 --> 00:11:16,399
- You, Mi Kyeong?
- Yes.

193
00:11:23,790 --> 00:11:28,128
Mr. Cho, is Prosecutor Kang really
here on Yeongseondo Island?

194
00:11:28,128 --> 00:11:31,330
But there's not even a trace of her.

195
00:11:32,090 --> 00:11:36,344
What, did you expect her
to suddenly pop up like in a movie?

196
00:11:36,344 --> 00:11:41,099
You know, tailing someone is all
about patience. It's a game of patience.

197
00:11:41,099 --> 00:11:45,270
Still though, finding a needle in a sand pit
might be easier.

198
00:11:45,270 --> 00:11:50,474
Patience, patience, patience.

199
00:11:50,474 --> 00:11:52,800
[Restricted number]

200
00:11:57,991 --> 00:12:00,327
Mr. Cho, I gotta take this call.
Be right back.

201
00:12:00,327 --> 00:12:02,028
Okay.

202
00:12:05,915 --> 00:12:07,292
Yes, go ahead, boss.

203
00:12:07,292 --> 00:12:08,793
It's nothing serious.

204
00:12:08,793 --> 00:12:12,005
You need to come visit me today.

205
00:12:12,005 --> 00:12:13,631
Suddenly? What for?

206
00:12:13,631 --> 00:12:16,760
What, you only come when something happened?

207
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:18,887
I'm also curious about how things are going

208
00:12:18,887 --> 00:12:21,213
with Prosecutor Kang.

209
00:12:21,973 --> 00:12:24,309
Why? Are you busy?

210
00:12:24,309 --> 00:12:26,186
No, boss. I'll come right away.

211
00:12:26,186 --> 00:12:29,013
Alright, don't be late.

212
00:12:38,239 --> 00:12:40,107
Oh, dear.

213
00:12:41,408 --> 00:12:44,353
Oh, my.

214
00:12:48,375 --> 00:12:50,335
Mr. Cho, I'm sorry,

215
00:12:50,335 --> 00:12:54,330
but you'll have to
check the CCTV alone today.

216
00:12:55,090 --> 00:12:57,249
Why? All of a sudden?

217
00:12:58,134 --> 00:13:02,722
It's just that
headquarters suddenly asked me to come in

218
00:13:02,722 --> 00:13:06,518
for organizing some inventory
at the convenience store.

219
00:13:06,518 --> 00:13:08,427
I'll be back quickly.

220
00:13:09,354 --> 00:13:11,439
Hurry back. My eyes can't take this for long.

221
00:13:11,439 --> 00:13:13,140
Okay.

222
00:13:38,716 --> 00:13:39,968
Director!

223
00:13:39,968 --> 00:13:42,545
I think you should take a look at this.

224
00:13:46,391 --> 00:13:47,600
- Here.
- What is it?

225
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:50,228
[Deposit Amount: 300,000,000 won]
We shouldn't receive such a large amount.

226
00:13:50,228 --> 00:13:52,856
Do you know anything about this?

227
00:13:52,856 --> 00:13:54,640
N-No...

228
00:13:57,056 --> 00:13:59,279
Where is Mr. Park?

229
00:13:59,279 --> 00:14:01,322
I was just about to tell you.

230
00:14:01,322 --> 00:14:04,692
Mr. Park is absent without notice today.

231
00:14:09,896 --> 00:14:11,168
[Mr. Park Sung Hwan]

232
00:14:15,336 --> 00:14:18,622
The subscriber you are calling
is not available.

233
00:14:21,551 --> 00:14:24,044
One bowl of rice soup, please.

234
00:14:28,099 --> 00:14:29,800
Okay.

235
00:14:31,144 --> 00:14:35,306
Huh? Why are you here,
Assemblyman Han Kyung Wook?

236
00:14:36,149 --> 00:14:39,027
Didn't we already finish talking?

237
00:14:39,027 --> 00:14:40,728
Take a look.

238
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,696
[Details on illegal political funding
at Ja Ae-won Orphanage]

239
00:15:01,184 --> 00:15:03,200
[Evidence of artwork reception
and fingerprint evidence material]

240
00:15:06,336 --> 00:15:07,520
[Bank transaction history
of Yeongseon Ja Ae-won Orphanage]

241
00:15:07,520 --> 00:15:08,704
[300,000,000 won]

242
00:15:15,104 --> 00:15:19,150
Are you trying to blackmail me
with fabricated evidence?

243
00:15:19,150 --> 00:15:21,402
Fabricated?

244
00:15:21,402 --> 00:15:24,781
Didn't your wife recently receive them?

245
00:15:24,781 --> 00:15:29,026
Various books and expensive artworks.

246
00:15:29,994 --> 00:15:33,873
- Don't tell me those were all...
- I never imagined that you,

247
00:15:33,873 --> 00:15:38,294
Candidate Kim Seon Jung,
a respected educator known for integrity,

248
00:15:38,294 --> 00:15:40,129
would even use your spouse

249
00:15:40,129 --> 00:15:44,050
to raise political funds like this.

250
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:46,302
You...

251
00:15:46,302 --> 00:15:48,846
If you resign now,

252
00:15:48,846 --> 00:15:51,766
this material won't be released to the press.

253
00:15:51,766 --> 00:15:56,646
And your spotless reputation
as a noble educator

254
00:15:56,646 --> 00:15:58,973
won't be tarnished at all.

255
00:16:01,901 --> 00:16:06,656
If I were afraid of a little damage
to my reputation,

256
00:16:06,656 --> 00:16:09,867
I wouldn't have run for office
in the first place.

257
00:16:09,867 --> 00:16:14,080
Seeing this only strengthens my resolve.

258
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:17,208
Even if I have to be covered in filth,

259
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:21,713
I'll stop a swindler like you
from becoming the mayor,

260
00:16:21,713 --> 00:16:23,872
Assemblyman Han.

261
00:16:29,596 --> 00:16:32,807
Perhaps you've lived too long

262
00:16:32,807 --> 00:16:35,602
in your world of pristine waters, Candidate.

263
00:16:35,602 --> 00:16:40,982
You can't seem to see what's really
lying at the bottom of the river.

264
00:16:40,982 --> 00:16:43,902
Do you know what I learned
after dealing with countless people

265
00:16:43,902 --> 00:16:46,061
in the intelligence service?

266
00:16:46,904 --> 00:16:50,533
To someone standing
before unbearable suffering,

267
00:16:50,533 --> 00:16:53,360
innocence means nothing.

268
00:16:54,454 --> 00:16:57,040
When this hits headlines,

269
00:16:57,040 --> 00:17:02,754
do you really think all you'll have to endure
is a little public criticism?

270
00:17:02,754 --> 00:17:05,256
Public opinion will only keep getting worse.

271
00:17:05,256 --> 00:17:08,551
No matter how loudly
you protest your innocence,

272
00:17:08,551 --> 00:17:10,803
do you think anyone will listen?

273
00:17:10,803 --> 00:17:12,597
Ja Ae-won Orphanage,
which you've cherished for years,

274
00:17:12,597 --> 00:17:16,392
will be branded a haven for illegal activity
and fall apart.

275
00:17:16,392 --> 00:17:19,145
And what about the people who support you?

276
00:17:19,145 --> 00:17:23,983
They'll be too afraid of being labeled
your accomplices to say a word.

277
00:17:23,983 --> 00:17:26,027
In the end,

278
00:17:26,027 --> 00:17:29,781
you'll spend years
trapped in endless court battles

279
00:17:29,781 --> 00:17:31,282
and end up walking in and out

280
00:17:31,282 --> 00:17:34,661
of detention centers
and prisons with your wife.

281
00:17:34,661 --> 00:17:36,287
I'm curious, though.

282
00:17:36,287 --> 00:17:39,040
After going through all of that,
Candidate Kim Seon Jung,

283
00:17:39,040 --> 00:17:42,293
do you really think you'll still be able

284
00:17:42,293 --> 00:17:44,671
to stand before me with your head held high

285
00:17:44,671 --> 00:17:47,664
and talk about justice and innocence?

286
00:17:49,717 --> 00:17:55,339
Because I've never met
a single person who could.

287
00:18:34,637 --> 00:18:37,849
But this Sergeant Kim,
he's with Yoo In Goo's crew, right?

288
00:18:37,849 --> 00:18:41,227
Right, a corrupt cop bought by Yoo In Goo.

289
00:18:41,227 --> 00:18:42,400
Then are you saying

290
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:45,565
Bulgae teamed up with Yoo In Goo
on top of helping Kim Seon Jung?

291
00:18:45,565 --> 00:18:48,985
Yoo In Goo was chasing him just yesterday,
and now they're allies?

292
00:18:48,985 --> 00:18:50,236
That doesn't make any sense.

293
00:18:50,236 --> 00:18:51,821
No.

294
00:18:51,821 --> 00:18:54,699
If that officer's involved,
it makes perfect sense.

295
00:18:54,699 --> 00:18:56,576
Honestly, I've always thought

296
00:18:56,576 --> 00:18:58,494
that police officer was suspicious.

297
00:18:58,494 --> 00:18:59,954
What made you think that?

298
00:18:59,954 --> 00:19:01,372
For three years,

299
00:19:01,372 --> 00:19:03,750
after every patrol, she'd come to
our convenience store

300
00:19:03,750 --> 00:19:05,209
and eat nothing but lunchboxes.

301
00:19:05,209 --> 00:19:07,462
But nobody can eat
convenience store lunchboxes

302
00:19:07,462 --> 00:19:09,505
every single day
without getting sick of them.

303
00:19:09,505 --> 00:19:11,799
I thought it was strange,

304
00:19:11,799 --> 00:19:15,595
and lately she's been throwing glances
at my boss.

305
00:19:15,595 --> 00:19:18,306
Honestly, a beauty like her

306
00:19:18,306 --> 00:19:21,225
showing interest in my boss
and visiting every day?

307
00:19:21,225 --> 00:19:22,894
That's just not believable.

308
00:19:22,894 --> 00:19:24,270
I've known him for over ten years,

309
00:19:24,270 --> 00:19:27,440
and even I get startled seeing him sometimes.

310
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,901
So she approached Kang Beom Ryong on purpose?

311
00:19:29,901 --> 00:19:32,737
She figured out he used to be
the second-in-command of the Hwasan faction

312
00:19:32,737 --> 00:19:35,522
and planned to use him from the start.

313
00:19:37,450 --> 00:19:41,454
But, you seem awfully excited
about this, huh?

314
00:19:41,454 --> 00:19:43,864
Are you happy your boss got played?

315
00:19:45,792 --> 00:19:48,336
No, it's not that.

316
00:19:48,336 --> 00:19:50,505
I'm worried about him. That's all.

317
00:19:50,505 --> 00:19:52,965
He could fall head over heels

318
00:19:52,965 --> 00:19:55,843
for a suspicious woman like that
and ruin his life.

319
00:19:55,843 --> 00:19:58,721
Anyway, we don't know anything for sure yet,
so let's keep watching.

320
00:19:58,721 --> 00:20:03,091
And don't let Kang Beom Ryong catch on
until we're certain.

321
00:20:04,393 --> 00:20:06,345
Alright then.

322
00:20:14,862 --> 00:20:17,198
Yesterday? It looked just like last time.

323
00:20:17,198 --> 00:20:20,493
You suddenly flipped out,
started doing those weird steps,

324
00:20:20,493 --> 00:20:22,444
and kicked everything in sight.

325
00:21:03,035 --> 00:21:04,861
What are you doing?

326
00:21:10,751 --> 00:21:14,496
I was trying different things
in case they triggered some memories.

327
00:21:15,423 --> 00:21:17,124
Oh.

328
00:21:19,135 --> 00:21:21,053
Want me to help?

329
00:21:21,053 --> 00:21:23,222
- Pardon?
- I mean...

330
00:21:23,222 --> 00:21:25,725
I may not look it,

331
00:21:25,725 --> 00:21:28,477
but before becoming a prosecutor,
I spent years in violent crimes.

332
00:21:28,477 --> 00:21:30,771
After handling so many cases,

333
00:21:30,771 --> 00:21:33,608
I can usually piece together someone's life

334
00:21:33,608 --> 00:21:37,194
just from their face, behavior,
or belongings.

335
00:21:37,194 --> 00:21:40,063
You can really do that?

336
00:21:40,740 --> 00:21:43,910
So, do you still have any belongings

337
00:21:43,910 --> 00:21:46,162
from when you were found
on the beach ten years ago?

338
00:21:46,162 --> 00:21:49,582
If I see them, I might be able to figure out

339
00:21:49,582 --> 00:21:52,451
what kind of person you used to be.

340
00:21:54,962 --> 00:21:56,872
My belongings?

341
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:00,160
[Full House]

342
00:22:03,296 --> 00:22:04,320
[Park Mi Kyeong]

343
00:22:11,812 --> 00:22:13,847
What now?

344
00:22:17,234 --> 00:22:20,404
You should carry out the mission
you've been assigned.

345
00:22:20,404 --> 00:22:22,114
Do I really have to?

346
00:22:22,114 --> 00:22:24,408
Can't fellow officers
cut each other some slack?

347
00:22:24,408 --> 00:22:26,077
Fellow officers?

348
00:22:26,077 --> 00:22:28,278
There are ranks among cops, you know.

349
00:22:32,875 --> 00:22:34,377
Oh, Sergeant Kim.

350
00:22:34,377 --> 00:22:36,045
I was just about to call you.

351
00:22:36,045 --> 00:22:39,090
Oh dear, boss. I should've called sooner.

352
00:22:39,090 --> 00:22:40,925
What happened with the deal yesterday?

353
00:22:40,925 --> 00:22:43,219
I heard things got pretty crazy
and all sorts of stuff went down.

354
00:22:43,219 --> 00:22:45,012
Jeez, the deal completely fell apart.

355
00:22:45,012 --> 00:22:47,515
- Things are a total mess over here.
- Oh, dear.

356
00:22:47,515 --> 00:22:49,841
Oh my, that's terrible.

357
00:22:51,394 --> 00:22:54,855
Anyway, I've got something
to tell you about that.

358
00:22:54,855 --> 00:22:56,691
You got time right now?

359
00:22:56,691 --> 00:22:59,309
Y-You want me there now?

360
00:23:00,569 --> 00:23:03,197
Yes, yes, I'll be there right away.

361
00:23:03,197 --> 00:23:06,742
But boss, I've got a junior
I recently brought in.

362
00:23:06,742 --> 00:23:09,194
Mind if she joins us?

363
00:23:09,870 --> 00:23:11,613
Yeah, boss.

364
00:23:19,755 --> 00:23:22,258
OH! There they are!

365
00:23:22,258 --> 00:23:24,885
Those dirty cops are on the move.
Something must be going on for sure.

366
00:23:24,885 --> 00:23:26,554
Hurry!

367
00:23:26,554 --> 00:23:28,139
- Start the car already!
- Oh, jeez.

368
00:23:28,139 --> 00:23:29,223
You're driving me crazy
with all that yelling.

369
00:23:29,223 --> 00:23:31,225
- I'm starting it already.
- Come on, hurry up!

370
00:23:31,225 --> 00:23:33,969
- We're gonna lose them!
- Put your seatbelt on.

371
00:23:38,441 --> 00:23:40,267
They're moving out now.

372
00:23:42,111 --> 00:23:43,487
Ah, step on it and catch up!

373
00:23:43,487 --> 00:23:45,605
Keep it down!

374
00:24:02,506 --> 00:24:04,258
Sorry, boss. I'm a little late!

375
00:24:04,258 --> 00:24:07,044
Why are you always late?

376
00:24:18,773 --> 00:24:20,474
Huh?

377
00:24:21,734 --> 00:24:23,736
Who's this?

378
00:24:23,736 --> 00:24:26,489
Introduce yourself. Go on.

379
00:24:26,489 --> 00:24:27,782
Nice to meet you.

380
00:24:27,782 --> 00:24:29,241
I'm Officer Park Mi Kyeong.

381
00:24:29,241 --> 00:24:32,953
Ah! So she's the junior you mentioned.

382
00:24:32,953 --> 00:24:34,330
Yes.

383
00:24:34,330 --> 00:24:35,956
She's sharp, so I thought she'd be useful.

384
00:24:35,956 --> 00:24:38,283
- That's why I brought her along.
- Yeah?

385
00:24:39,835 --> 00:24:42,505
Hello, I'm Geum Kang Sik.

386
00:24:42,505 --> 00:24:44,632
Hello.

387
00:24:44,632 --> 00:24:47,084
You've got great manners, as always.

388
00:24:50,596 --> 00:24:52,681
But why did you ask us to meet at the harbor?

389
00:24:52,681 --> 00:24:54,058
You said the deal fell through.

390
00:24:54,058 --> 00:24:56,102
Exactly because it fell through.

391
00:24:56,102 --> 00:25:00,231
You and your junior need to do a little work.

392
00:25:00,231 --> 00:25:03,984
You know all the dashcam and CCTV footage
from around here last night?

393
00:25:03,984 --> 00:25:06,904
I want you to gather every last bit of it.

394
00:25:06,904 --> 00:25:08,447
Huh? Why?

395
00:25:08,447 --> 00:25:10,491
Man, you sure ask a lot of questions.

396
00:25:10,491 --> 00:25:12,201
There are guys who messed up
the deal yesterday.

397
00:25:12,201 --> 00:25:15,704
We've got special orders
to find out who they are, okay?

398
00:25:15,704 --> 00:25:16,956
If we dig through enough footage,

399
00:25:16,956 --> 00:25:18,415
we'll at least figure out where they went.

400
00:25:18,415 --> 00:25:20,116
Ugh, seriously.

401
00:25:21,210 --> 00:25:23,629
By the way, you can handle this, right?

402
00:25:23,629 --> 00:25:27,216
You're a new face,
so it makes me a bit worried.

403
00:25:27,216 --> 00:25:28,843
Patrol work is my specialty.

404
00:25:28,843 --> 00:25:31,011
No need to worry.

405
00:25:31,011 --> 00:25:32,179
Wow!

406
00:25:32,179 --> 00:25:33,764
Patrol work is her specialty?

407
00:25:33,764 --> 00:25:35,015
Specialty? Okay!

408
00:25:35,015 --> 00:25:38,227
Then put that talent to good use
and find something.

409
00:25:38,227 --> 00:25:41,021
Then I'll get you a proper incentive.

410
00:25:41,021 --> 00:25:42,815
Oh! Incentive, incentive!

411
00:25:42,815 --> 00:25:44,942
Mr. Yoo really knows how to reward people.

412
00:25:44,942 --> 00:25:46,610
What do you mean Mr. Yoo?

413
00:25:46,610 --> 00:25:48,737
This must never reach Mr. Yoo's ears.

414
00:25:48,737 --> 00:25:52,440
What? Isn't this Mr. Yoo's order?

415
00:25:53,409 --> 00:25:55,286
Listen carefully, okay?

416
00:25:55,286 --> 00:25:57,413
Mr. Yoo is finished now.

417
00:25:57,413 --> 00:25:59,748
If you don't want to
get dragged down with him,

418
00:25:59,748 --> 00:26:00,916
delete his number first.

419
00:26:00,916 --> 00:26:03,252
And if he calls, don't answer. Got it?

420
00:26:03,252 --> 00:26:04,628
Yeah, okay.

421
00:26:04,628 --> 00:26:08,540
Then who gave this special order?

422
00:26:09,300 --> 00:26:11,844
Chairman Do of Heaven Casino.

423
00:26:11,844 --> 00:26:13,628
You wouldn't know him.

424
00:26:20,644 --> 00:26:23,314
Those guys seem to be tracing us.

425
00:26:23,314 --> 00:26:25,232
What if they've caught onto something?

426
00:26:25,232 --> 00:26:28,944
We followed the route I planned.
How would they know anything?

427
00:26:28,944 --> 00:26:31,021
You never know.

428
00:26:32,823 --> 00:26:34,033
That officer.

429
00:26:34,033 --> 00:26:35,743
Instead of just watching her,

430
00:26:35,743 --> 00:26:38,412
shouldn't we make a move first?

431
00:26:38,412 --> 00:26:40,497
I told you already.

432
00:26:40,497 --> 00:26:43,450
Our target is Bulgae, not that officer.

433
00:26:44,251 --> 00:26:46,712
Just sit tight and watch!

434
00:26:46,712 --> 00:26:48,997
You have no patience.

435
00:26:53,177 --> 00:26:55,086
No patience?

436
00:26:56,180 --> 00:26:59,516
Mr. Jeong, I think you've got the wrong idea.

437
00:26:59,516 --> 00:27:03,729
Beom Ryong and I have spent ten years
preparing to avenge our boss.

438
00:27:03,729 --> 00:27:07,015
Always enduring, waiting, and holding back...

439
00:27:08,067 --> 00:27:09,610
Jeez, how admirable.

440
00:27:09,610 --> 00:27:11,978
What's so special about that boss of yours?

441
00:27:13,155 --> 00:27:15,783
Mr. Jeong, say what you want in front of me,

442
00:27:15,783 --> 00:27:18,827
but don't talk about him like that
in front of Beom Ryong.

443
00:27:18,827 --> 00:27:20,746
To Beom Ryong, he's not just a boss.

444
00:27:20,746 --> 00:27:24,959
He's the mentor he respects
and the father who took him in.

445
00:27:24,959 --> 00:27:26,502
If anyone goes against him

446
00:27:26,502 --> 00:27:28,420
or insults him in front of Beom Ryong,

447
00:27:28,420 --> 00:27:32,216
that's the day a war starts, understand?

448
00:27:32,216 --> 00:27:34,093
How foolish.

449
00:27:34,093 --> 00:27:36,929
You think your boss in prison will appreciate

450
00:27:36,929 --> 00:27:39,765
all that loyalty and devotion?

451
00:27:39,765 --> 00:27:44,645
You know, people never see
utterly loyal subordinates as equals.

452
00:27:44,645 --> 00:27:47,022
They see them as obedient dogs.

453
00:27:47,022 --> 00:27:50,025
Speaking from experience?
Why are you so cynical?

454
00:27:50,025 --> 00:27:52,861
Sounds like someone
really did a number on you.

455
00:27:52,861 --> 00:27:57,116
I'm giving you this advice as an NIS agent
who's been through it all.

456
00:27:57,116 --> 00:27:58,984
Be careful.

457
00:28:10,629 --> 00:28:13,382
Boss, is something wrong?

458
00:28:13,382 --> 00:28:14,967
Nothing's wrong.

459
00:28:14,967 --> 00:28:18,044
I just wanted to see your face.

460
00:28:18,679 --> 00:28:22,215
Is everything moving along smoothly
with Prosecutor Kang?

461
00:28:23,559 --> 00:28:25,019
Yes.

462
00:28:25,019 --> 00:28:26,520
No major problems so far?

463
00:28:26,520 --> 00:28:28,480
Well, not yet.

464
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:30,941
Things haven't settled enough
for a proper report,

465
00:28:30,941 --> 00:28:33,518
so I'll tell you once things are clearer.

466
00:28:34,236 --> 00:28:37,656
Guess I'm bothering you while you're busy.

467
00:28:37,656 --> 00:28:39,199
No, boss. Not at all.

468
00:28:39,199 --> 00:28:43,037
Maybe it's because I've been locked up
for so long and gotten lonely,

469
00:28:43,037 --> 00:28:46,999
but I've been thinking a lot
about the old days lately.

470
00:28:46,999 --> 00:28:51,086
Do you remember
how many people stabbed me in the back

471
00:28:51,086 --> 00:28:52,921
- over the last thirty years?
- Twelve.

472
00:28:52,921 --> 00:28:55,123
That's right. Twelve.

473
00:28:56,008 --> 00:28:59,011
One of them was a friend
I'd known for forty years.

474
00:28:59,011 --> 00:29:02,547
Another was like a son
who followed me like I was his father.

475
00:29:04,683 --> 00:29:06,894
After being betrayed by those people,

476
00:29:06,894 --> 00:29:09,855
ending up living like this,

477
00:29:09,855 --> 00:29:15,602
I can't help but wonder
if I've lived my life all wrong.

478
00:29:16,779 --> 00:29:19,156
- It's got me uneasy.
- No, boss.

479
00:29:19,156 --> 00:29:21,149
Absolutely not.

480
00:29:22,201 --> 00:29:24,828
But when I think about it,

481
00:29:24,828 --> 00:29:26,663
even though twelve betrayed me,

482
00:29:26,663 --> 00:29:30,417
one man, Kang Beom Ryong,

483
00:29:30,417 --> 00:29:34,129
stood by me as if he were a hundred men.

484
00:29:34,129 --> 00:29:37,332
You have no idea how reassuring that is.

485
00:29:38,342 --> 00:29:41,887
So what else can I do?

486
00:29:41,887 --> 00:29:44,473
So here I am, a man who doubts everyone,

487
00:29:44,473 --> 00:29:46,892
who can't even trust
his own wife or children,

488
00:29:46,892 --> 00:29:50,929
yet I trust you, Kang Beom Ryong, completely.

489
00:29:53,732 --> 00:29:56,235
Leave it to me.

490
00:29:56,235 --> 00:29:59,780
Beom Ryong, from now on,

491
00:29:59,780 --> 00:30:04,535
you're the only one I'm counting on.

492
00:30:04,535 --> 00:30:06,236
You know that, right?

493
00:30:07,830 --> 00:30:09,739
Yes, I understand.

494
00:30:21,009 --> 00:30:22,845
From now on,

495
00:30:22,845 --> 00:30:26,422
you're the only one I'm counting on.

496
00:30:27,433 --> 00:30:29,435
What?

497
00:30:29,435 --> 00:30:31,136
I'm sorry.

498
00:30:34,064 --> 00:30:40,103
Looks like things didn't go so well
with your subordinate.

499
00:31:12,644 --> 00:31:18,692
So these are... the clothes you were wearing

500
00:31:18,692 --> 00:31:21,487
when you fell into the water,
Ms. Bong Jae Soon?

501
00:31:21,487 --> 00:31:22,863
Yes.

502
00:31:22,863 --> 00:31:29,824
But, why were you wearing these, Jae Soon?

503
00:31:29,824 --> 00:31:31,580
Oh, jeez.

504
00:31:31,580 --> 00:31:34,082
Just to be clear,
this has absolutely nothing to do

505
00:31:34,082 --> 00:31:35,501
with my personal taste.

506
00:31:35,501 --> 00:31:37,920
I genuinely have no interest
in women's clothes like this.

507
00:31:37,920 --> 00:31:40,923
But no matter how much
I look at these, I can't remember

508
00:31:40,923 --> 00:31:43,217
why I ended up in the sea wearing these.

509
00:31:43,217 --> 00:31:44,959
Okay.

510
00:31:45,886 --> 00:31:50,182
Then... were there any other belongings?

511
00:31:50,182 --> 00:31:54,561
According to the old man,
there was only an ID and a photograph.

512
00:31:54,561 --> 00:31:58,941
I've checked the records, turns out I have
no family and no one looking for me.

513
00:31:58,941 --> 00:32:00,734
What about the photo?

514
00:32:00,734 --> 00:32:02,518
Even the photo...

515
00:32:05,364 --> 00:32:08,659
I can't tell what it is
no matter how many times I look at it.

516
00:32:08,659 --> 00:32:11,537
It looks like it could be
from a postcard or a magazine.

517
00:32:11,537 --> 00:32:14,030
What does it look like to you, Prosecutor?

518
00:32:14,748 --> 00:32:16,375
What if...

519
00:32:16,375 --> 00:32:18,502
What would you do

520
00:32:18,502 --> 00:32:23,549
if everything you thought you knew
about your past was wrong?

521
00:32:23,549 --> 00:32:25,175
- Pardon?
- Well, it's possible, isn't it?

522
00:32:25,175 --> 00:32:28,345
So like, what if you found out
you were a serial killer?

523
00:32:28,345 --> 00:32:29,555
Or something equally shocking.

524
00:32:29,555 --> 00:32:32,715
Even so, do you still want to
find out about your past?

525
00:32:37,771 --> 00:32:41,692
I've thought about the possibility
that it might be hard to accept.

526
00:32:41,692 --> 00:32:46,062
Still, if I can,
I'd like to find out the truth.

527
00:32:46,738 --> 00:32:49,983
Because my past is part of who I am.

528
00:32:51,743 --> 00:32:53,987
I've already made up my mind.

529
00:32:54,788 --> 00:32:57,991
No matter what I was like in the past,

530
00:32:59,001 --> 00:33:04,789
I want to make an effort
to try and accept it.

531
00:33:27,404 --> 00:33:30,231
Then I'll get going first.

532
00:33:43,295 --> 00:33:45,756
No need to sit. This won't take long.

533
00:33:45,756 --> 00:33:47,457
Pardon?

534
00:33:53,597 --> 00:33:55,140
I've committed an unforgivable mistake!

535
00:33:55,140 --> 00:33:57,643
- I'll explain everything!
- An explanation

536
00:33:57,643 --> 00:34:00,270
doesn't turn failure into success.

537
00:34:00,270 --> 00:34:02,648
- Mr. Han...
- Honestly, I don't care

538
00:34:02,648 --> 00:34:05,567
whether you sell drugs
or kill prosecutors, Mr. Yoo.

539
00:34:05,567 --> 00:34:08,320
As long as the job gets done

540
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:11,281
and leaves no loose ends,

541
00:34:11,281 --> 00:34:17,779
I could overlook
a certain amount of freelancing. But...

542
00:34:20,374 --> 00:34:23,502
How did you manage
to screw things up this badly?

543
00:34:23,502 --> 00:34:24,920
I'll fix everything.

544
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:27,589
I'll track down and crush those masked punks
who ruined the drug deal,

545
00:34:27,589 --> 00:34:29,049
and get back the money--

546
00:34:29,049 --> 00:34:32,177
Not fix it.

547
00:34:32,177 --> 00:34:34,670
You need to take responsibility.

548
00:34:37,849 --> 00:34:40,018
Give up every business connected to you,

549
00:34:40,018 --> 00:34:41,844
and hand them over to Chairman Do.

550
00:34:42,896 --> 00:34:45,107
Mr. Han, how can I hand over my businesses
to Chairman Do?

551
00:34:45,107 --> 00:34:46,400
I think there's been a misunderstanding.

552
00:34:46,400 --> 00:34:47,526
Mr. Han is done with you.

553
00:34:47,526 --> 00:34:50,269
- Leave now!
- This is completely unfair.

554
00:34:55,784 --> 00:34:57,703
Unfair?

555
00:34:57,703 --> 00:34:59,955
Yeah, I've heard it enough to be sick of it.

556
00:34:59,955 --> 00:35:02,874
"It's unfair. I did nothing wrong."

557
00:35:02,874 --> 00:35:05,168
You know what all those guys have in common?

558
00:35:05,168 --> 00:35:06,962
Give me two hours alone with them,

559
00:35:06,962 --> 00:35:09,464
and the color drains
right out of their faces.

560
00:35:09,464 --> 00:35:14,177
Then they start begging for their lives
like nothing has happened

561
00:35:14,177 --> 00:35:17,130
and rattling off every wrong
they've ever done.

562
00:35:21,184 --> 00:35:23,219
What do you think you'll do?

563
00:35:32,195 --> 00:35:34,114
Secretary Baek.

564
00:35:34,114 --> 00:35:36,158
Let me ask you just one thing.

565
00:35:36,158 --> 00:35:39,652
Was this whole thing
orchestrated by Do Hyeon Tae?

566
00:35:56,762 --> 00:35:58,722
- Kang Sik.
- Yes.

567
00:35:58,722 --> 00:36:00,348
Get all our boys together.

568
00:36:00,348 --> 00:36:02,851
Boss, what are you planning to do?

569
00:36:02,851 --> 00:36:05,812
The coffin lid isn't shut yet.
Shouldn't we at least fight before it's over?

570
00:36:05,812 --> 00:36:07,522
Tonight, we're going after Chairman Do.

571
00:36:07,522 --> 00:36:09,357
Boss, it's too dangerous.

572
00:36:09,357 --> 00:36:11,276
Danger or not, my hard-earned business

573
00:36:11,276 --> 00:36:13,153
has already been completely handed over
to Chairman Do.

574
00:36:13,153 --> 00:36:14,154
If I just let this happen,

575
00:36:14,154 --> 00:36:16,490
how am I supposed to show my face
in this world?

576
00:36:16,490 --> 00:36:19,493
I'll take down Chairman Do,
get my businesses back,

577
00:36:19,493 --> 00:36:22,579
and settle things with Mr. Han too.

578
00:36:22,579 --> 00:36:24,623
You understand?

579
00:36:24,623 --> 00:36:27,167
Understood, boss. I'll get the boys ready.

580
00:36:27,167 --> 00:36:31,204
Good. I'll show them
what kind of man I really am.

581
00:36:40,180 --> 00:36:41,881
You must be tired.

582
00:36:42,933 --> 00:36:46,019
That idiot Yoo In Goo has made things
unnecessarily complicated.

583
00:36:46,019 --> 00:36:47,771
He's going to cause us
a lot of headaches going forward.

584
00:36:47,771 --> 00:36:50,106
As for the businesses,
Chairman Do will manage them well, right?

585
00:36:50,106 --> 00:36:54,227
Chairman Do is useless
for anything outside business.

586
00:36:55,153 --> 00:36:59,491
Yoo In Goo was at least
good for handling the dirty work.

587
00:36:59,491 --> 00:37:01,284
Didn't Chairman Do say

588
00:37:01,284 --> 00:37:03,286
he'd place a capable replacement
under Yoo In Goo?

589
00:37:03,286 --> 00:37:07,999
If we want the Yeongseondo Island Project
to go smoothly to the end,

590
00:37:07,999 --> 00:37:10,284
those kinds of people won't cut it.

591
00:37:13,004 --> 00:37:15,715
We need a seasoned veteran

592
00:37:15,715 --> 00:37:19,085
who's survived a few battlefields.

593
00:37:25,632 --> 00:37:30,336
[Sending you materials
related to the ferry incident]

594
00:37:42,659 --> 00:37:44,360
Wow.

595
00:37:45,662 --> 00:37:48,081
So it wasn't an unidentified woman,

596
00:37:48,081 --> 00:37:50,616
it was Mr. Bong Jae Soon.

597
00:37:56,381 --> 00:37:58,082
North Korea...

598
00:37:58,082 --> 00:37:59,264
[Two NIS agents vanished
during a ferry arrest operation]

599
00:37:59,264 --> 00:38:00,385
[before making contact with North Korea]

600
00:38:00,385 --> 00:38:02,420
NIS...

601
00:38:07,726 --> 00:38:12,230
Today is the day that decides
whether the In Goo faction lives or dies.

602
00:38:12,230 --> 00:38:14,065
Will we live with everything taken away

603
00:38:14,065 --> 00:38:16,109
by that fox Chairman Do
and be looked down on forever,

604
00:38:16,109 --> 00:38:19,654
or will we rise again with me?

605
00:38:19,654 --> 00:38:22,365
That's up to all of you.

606
00:38:22,365 --> 00:38:25,026
- Understood?
- Yes, boss!

607
00:38:26,494 --> 00:38:28,195
Boss.

608
00:38:29,873 --> 00:38:33,668
- Chairman Do is currently at the penthouse.
- What about security?

609
00:38:33,668 --> 00:38:37,297
I've confirmed that Mr. Nam
and everyone else have left for the day.

610
00:38:37,297 --> 00:38:38,998
Let's go.

611
00:39:27,055 --> 00:39:28,139
Wow!

612
00:39:28,139 --> 00:39:30,433
Nice timing, Mr. Yoo. You came just in time.

613
00:39:30,433 --> 00:39:33,269
What are you up to now?
Can't you read the room?

614
00:39:33,269 --> 00:39:35,397
Come on, of course I can.

615
00:39:35,397 --> 00:39:38,608
I've got the whole situation figured out.

616
00:39:38,608 --> 00:39:40,860
You're here to stab me in the back,
aren't you?

617
00:39:40,860 --> 00:39:44,063
And knowing that, you're popping champagne?

618
00:39:46,491 --> 00:39:48,192
Here.

619
00:40:01,715 --> 00:40:06,803
It's a historic moment, upgrading
from In Goo faction to Kang Sik faction.

620
00:40:06,803 --> 00:40:08,555
Can't let that pass without notice.

621
00:40:08,555 --> 00:40:12,350
A toast to the successful launch
of Kang Sik faction! Salute!

622
00:40:12,350 --> 00:40:14,135
Salute.

623
00:40:15,395 --> 00:40:17,230
Kang Sik, what are you up to?

624
00:40:17,230 --> 00:40:19,524
Salute.

625
00:40:19,524 --> 00:40:22,444
Mr. Yoo, can you not tell what's going on?

626
00:40:22,444 --> 00:40:27,106
Who do you think handed me
that dashcam SD card?

627
00:40:30,577 --> 00:40:32,662
You little rat, Geum Kang Sik!

628
00:40:32,662 --> 00:40:35,582
- How dare you do this to me?
- Why the harsh words?

629
00:40:35,582 --> 00:40:38,168
Mr. In Goo, I can't spend my whole life

630
00:40:38,168 --> 00:40:40,628
getting my shins kicked by you.

631
00:40:40,628 --> 00:40:42,797
I'm getting old enough for my bones to ache.

632
00:40:42,797 --> 00:40:46,333
Time for me to go independent, right?

633
00:40:49,304 --> 00:40:51,005
Boys.

634
00:40:53,058 --> 00:40:55,769
Do you really think
you'll get away with this?

635
00:40:55,769 --> 00:40:57,020
Mr. Geum? No, no.

636
00:40:57,020 --> 00:40:59,064
It's President Geum now.

637
00:40:59,064 --> 00:41:01,232
It's getting late,
so let's send Mr. Yoo on his way

638
00:41:01,232 --> 00:41:02,901
and sit down for a drink.

639
00:41:02,901 --> 00:41:04,069
- Yes.
- Come on, have a seat.

640
00:41:04,069 --> 00:41:05,320
Guys, what are you waiting for?

641
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:08,448
Mr. In Goo is heading somewhere nice.
See him off properly.

642
00:41:08,448 --> 00:41:09,824
Hey.

643
00:41:09,824 --> 00:41:11,525
Wait, wait.

644
00:41:15,789 --> 00:41:19,533
Let me say one thing. Okay?

645
00:41:31,096 --> 00:41:34,974
Looks like Kang Sik learned well under me.

646
00:41:34,974 --> 00:41:37,468
Even learned how to stab his boss
in the back.

647
00:41:38,895 --> 00:41:43,108
Chairman Do, I'm leaving anyway,

648
00:41:43,108 --> 00:41:47,028
but surely, one last glass of champagne
isn't too much to ask, right?

649
00:41:47,028 --> 00:41:49,197
Champagne, my foot.

650
00:41:49,197 --> 00:41:51,699
What kind of trick
are you trying to pull, Mr. In Goo?

651
00:41:51,699 --> 00:41:55,453
What trick? I'm about to take a long trip.
My throat's dry, that's all.

652
00:41:55,453 --> 00:41:58,531
Just one drink. Come on, don't be scared.

653
00:41:59,666 --> 00:42:03,786
Chairman Do, you've always been this timid?

654
00:42:04,712 --> 00:42:06,631
Trying to be clever, huh?

655
00:42:06,631 --> 00:42:09,384
Okay, okay.

656
00:42:09,384 --> 00:42:11,928
Mr. Yoo and I go way back.

657
00:42:11,928 --> 00:42:14,588
We should at least have a farewell drink.

658
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:18,717
Here. Goodbye.

659
00:42:36,286 --> 00:42:38,070
Oh, come on.

660
00:42:43,710 --> 00:42:45,744
Oh, jeez.

661
00:43:02,312 --> 00:43:05,014
Come on, don't be scared.

662
00:43:18,036 --> 00:43:21,664
Huh?

663
00:43:21,664 --> 00:43:24,083
Boss, boss!

664
00:43:24,083 --> 00:43:27,212
- Stop right there!
- Put the knife down!

665
00:43:27,212 --> 00:43:28,913
Put it down!

666
00:43:30,673 --> 00:43:32,383
Not putting it down?
I'm really gonna stab him.

667
00:43:32,383 --> 00:43:33,984
Do you really want me to stab him?

668
00:43:33,984 --> 00:43:35,094
- Put it down?
- Put it down.

669
00:43:35,094 --> 00:43:37,630
- Down, down!
- Told you to put it down.

670
00:43:38,723 --> 00:43:40,975
- Kang Sik.
- Yes, Boss In Goo.

671
00:43:40,975 --> 00:43:43,019
- Before I come back,
- Yes.

672
00:43:43,019 --> 00:43:45,846
- take good care of those shins of yours.
- Pardon?

673
00:43:50,401 --> 00:43:52,186
Go after him!

674
00:43:54,864 --> 00:43:56,157
Wow!

675
00:43:56,157 --> 00:44:00,078
- As expected, he never fails to surprise.
- Hurry!

676
00:44:00,078 --> 00:44:04,239
But what am I supposed to do
for fun without him?

677
00:44:19,847 --> 00:44:21,224
Hey, you punk!

678
00:44:21,224 --> 00:44:24,051
Get him!

679
00:44:32,160 --> 00:44:34,277
Get him!

680
00:44:44,032 --> 00:44:45,880
- Darn it.
- Come on!

681
00:44:50,080 --> 00:44:51,808
No...

682
00:44:52,797 --> 00:44:54,507
Geum Kang Sik!

683
00:44:54,507 --> 00:44:57,793
Do Hyeon Tae, Han Kyung Wook, those punks!

684
00:45:01,222 --> 00:45:04,642
Boss, what do we do?

685
00:45:04,642 --> 00:45:06,769
He can run all he wants,
but he's still stuck on the island.

686
00:45:06,769 --> 00:45:10,264
Without a penny to his name,
where could he possibly go?

687
00:45:11,107 --> 00:45:13,401
Station men at the terminal

688
00:45:13,401 --> 00:45:15,028
and search every place he might go.

689
00:45:15,028 --> 00:45:16,729
Yes, boss.

690
00:45:17,408 --> 00:45:19,919
[O Ran Chinese Restaurant]

691
00:45:27,040 --> 00:45:31,252
O Ran, do you have to go out again today?

692
00:45:31,252 --> 00:45:32,670
Why?

693
00:45:32,670 --> 00:45:34,088
Well, it's not that...

694
00:45:34,088 --> 00:45:37,425
It's just we're fully booked
with a group reservation today.

695
00:45:37,425 --> 00:45:39,302
No, no. The two of us can...

696
00:45:39,302 --> 00:45:40,928
- The two of us can...
- Enough!

697
00:45:40,928 --> 00:45:42,921
Don't hold back, just say it.

698
00:45:43,639 --> 00:45:45,933
This is getting ridiculous, don't you think?

699
00:45:45,933 --> 00:45:48,061
Huh? Ho Myung is gone,

700
00:45:48,061 --> 00:45:50,355
and you're always running around outside.

701
00:45:50,355 --> 00:45:53,733
Do you know how hard
Mr. Kim and I have been working?

702
00:45:53,733 --> 00:45:54,942
Do I really have to

703
00:45:54,942 --> 00:45:58,353
spend my old age walking on eggshells
around my daughter?

704
00:46:00,406 --> 00:46:03,201
Alright, I got it.

705
00:46:03,201 --> 00:46:05,119
I'll stay at the restaurant all day today.

706
00:46:05,119 --> 00:46:08,206
I'll handle everything myself,
from opening to closing.

707
00:46:08,206 --> 00:46:10,750
You two don't lift a finger.

708
00:46:10,750 --> 00:46:12,210
Just sit and rest today.

709
00:46:12,210 --> 00:46:14,128
Really? You're serious, right?

710
00:46:14,128 --> 00:46:17,548
Of course, I am. I wasn't planning
to go out today anyway.

711
00:46:17,548 --> 00:46:20,084
You two are taking the day off.

712
00:46:26,933 --> 00:46:29,143
Wait a second. What am I... Ah!

713
00:46:29,143 --> 00:46:31,562
- How about a cup of instant coffee first?
- Sit down. Stay seated.

714
00:46:31,562 --> 00:46:34,023
Why are you so quick on your feet
all of a sudden?

715
00:46:34,023 --> 00:46:37,226
I'll make it for you. I will.

716
00:46:38,569 --> 00:46:41,313
- Wait.
- You like that so much?

717
00:46:43,533 --> 00:46:46,160
We'll bring you breaking news
that just came in.

718
00:46:46,160 --> 00:46:49,580
Candidate Kim Seon Jung, who was leading
the Imcheon mayoral race,

719
00:46:49,580 --> 00:46:51,916
has just announced his voluntary withdrawal.

720
00:46:51,916 --> 00:46:53,668
While Candidate Kim cited

721
00:46:53,668 --> 00:46:55,837
[Imcheon mayoral candidate withdraws today]
health reasons for his resignation,

722
00:46:55,837 --> 00:47:00,967
the abrupt move has sparked
mixed reactions among his supporters.

723
00:47:00,967 --> 00:47:05,596
I once again apologize to my supporters

724
00:47:05,596 --> 00:47:08,307
and bow my head in sincere gratitude

725
00:47:08,307 --> 00:47:12,302
- for all the support I have received.
- Jeez!

726
00:47:13,187 --> 00:47:15,606
Have you looked into
the other thing I mentioned yesterday?

727
00:47:15,606 --> 00:47:17,066
The police are conducting a thorough search

728
00:47:17,066 --> 00:47:19,652
for the martial arts master

729
00:47:19,652 --> 00:47:22,530
and those masked guys.

730
00:47:22,530 --> 00:47:25,533
And regarding the Ja Ae-won Orphanage staff,

731
00:47:25,533 --> 00:47:27,410
I've put a few people on them.

732
00:47:27,410 --> 00:47:30,204
Whoever... Whoever they are,

733
00:47:30,204 --> 00:47:32,582
they'll contact us immediately upon approach.

734
00:47:32,582 --> 00:47:35,293
Good job, good job.
As expected of our Mr. Geum.

735
00:47:35,293 --> 00:47:39,255
No, President Geum,
you and I work perfectly in sync.

736
00:47:39,255 --> 00:47:40,715
I knew it would be like this.

737
00:47:40,715 --> 00:47:42,749
Eat this quickly. It's premium stuff.

738
00:47:50,224 --> 00:47:52,059
Step on it, harder!

739
00:47:52,059 --> 00:47:54,562
This stain won't come out at all.

740
00:47:54,562 --> 00:47:56,606
What is this? It's like being a slave.

741
00:47:56,606 --> 00:47:59,150
We should wash the blankets in the machine.

742
00:47:59,150 --> 00:48:00,693
How is anyone supposed to...

743
00:48:00,693 --> 00:48:04,021
Nam Il, step on the end a bit more.

744
00:48:05,239 --> 00:48:06,574
Oh, dear.

745
00:48:06,574 --> 00:48:08,868
You've really been working hard
since this morning.

746
00:48:08,868 --> 00:48:10,119
Prosecutor Kang,

747
00:48:10,119 --> 00:48:12,121
you're going back to the district
on the boat today, right?

748
00:48:12,121 --> 00:48:14,957
Yes. But it's the evening boat.

749
00:48:14,957 --> 00:48:16,375
You're not going to pretend
none of this happened

750
00:48:16,375 --> 00:48:17,960
just because you're leaving, right?

751
00:48:17,960 --> 00:48:20,421
Come on, I'll go back first,

752
00:48:20,421 --> 00:48:23,165
wrap up the urgent matters,
and come right back.

753
00:48:24,842 --> 00:48:27,220
- Are you busy?
- Pardon?

754
00:48:27,220 --> 00:48:30,297
There's something
I need to tell you before I leave.

755
00:48:31,224 --> 00:48:34,009
Oh, yes, go ahead and say it here.

756
00:48:38,064 --> 00:48:40,149
No, it's important,
so let's talk at the café.

757
00:48:40,149 --> 00:48:42,151
I'll wait downstairs, so come out.

758
00:48:42,151 --> 00:48:44,278
I'll step out for a moment.

759
00:48:44,278 --> 00:48:46,188
Okay, okay.

760
00:48:49,784 --> 00:48:51,744
Uncle, what's going on?

761
00:48:51,744 --> 00:48:53,371
Did something happen
with that prosecutor lady?

762
00:48:53,371 --> 00:48:55,540
She said she has something important to say
and wants to meet at the café.

763
00:48:55,540 --> 00:48:58,834
Right? I told you so!

764
00:48:58,834 --> 00:49:01,546
Her eyes looked serious, I'm telling you.

765
00:49:01,546 --> 00:49:03,005
It's not like that.

766
00:49:03,005 --> 00:49:06,175
But why is she suddenly asking to meet?

767
00:49:06,175 --> 00:49:08,919
Wait, wait, Uncle, hold on.

768
00:49:12,056 --> 00:49:13,266
You're not going to meet her
looking like that, are you?

769
00:49:13,266 --> 00:49:16,811
Right, a woman basically asked you out,
and you show up looking like that?

770
00:49:16,811 --> 00:49:19,105
It's not like she asked me out on a date.

771
00:49:19,105 --> 00:49:20,806
Well...

772
00:49:20,806 --> 00:49:24,448
[Jeongseok Study Residence]

773
00:49:39,328 --> 00:49:42,240
[One heart]

774
00:50:07,361 --> 00:50:09,146
Nam Il told me...

775
00:50:11,198 --> 00:50:12,825
to bundle up because it's cold.

776
00:50:12,825 --> 00:50:15,119
He even gave me a cap.

777
00:50:15,119 --> 00:50:17,321
- Looks weird, right?
- No.

778
00:50:19,206 --> 00:50:20,907
It's cute, though.

779
00:50:22,460 --> 00:50:24,161
Let's go.

780
00:50:32,094 --> 00:50:33,929
Director!

781
00:50:33,929 --> 00:50:35,765
- O Ran!
- What happened?

782
00:50:35,765 --> 00:50:37,141
Why is Mr. Kim resigning?

783
00:50:37,141 --> 00:50:38,842
What should I do?

784
00:50:41,604 --> 00:50:43,439
It's all my fault.

785
00:50:43,439 --> 00:50:46,901
I didn't even realize
they bribed my staff to get to him.

786
00:50:46,901 --> 00:50:49,695
He told me Chairman Do was suspicious

787
00:50:49,695 --> 00:50:52,606
and not to accept anything,

788
00:50:53,366 --> 00:50:54,825
but I was so foolish...

789
00:50:54,825 --> 00:50:56,410
No, wait.

790
00:50:56,410 --> 00:50:58,820
Please calm down, Director.

791
00:51:01,082 --> 00:51:03,125
I don't have time for this.

792
00:51:03,125 --> 00:51:05,753
O Ran, I'm sorry,
but I have to go out right now.

793
00:51:05,753 --> 00:51:07,880
- We'll talk details later.
- No, wait.

794
00:51:07,880 --> 00:51:09,382
But what are you going to do out there?

795
00:51:09,382 --> 00:51:12,093
That staff member has worked with me
for over ten years.

796
00:51:12,093 --> 00:51:13,928
If I go and talk to him,

797
00:51:13,928 --> 00:51:16,806
he'll come clean
and say it was all his doing,

798
00:51:16,806 --> 00:51:18,599
that my husband had nothing to do with it.

799
00:51:18,599 --> 00:51:21,769
But if they went as far as
bribing and threatening your staff,

800
00:51:21,769 --> 00:51:23,479
they're not ordinary people.

801
00:51:23,479 --> 00:51:25,356
I'll find a way to handle this.

802
00:51:25,356 --> 00:51:28,526
Please stay here and wait.

803
00:51:28,526 --> 00:51:30,778
Wait for what?

804
00:51:30,778 --> 00:51:35,116
If we lose time,
he can't even withdraw his resignation!

805
00:51:35,116 --> 00:51:39,161
Should he really give up the election
unfairly because of me?

806
00:51:39,161 --> 00:51:40,454
O Ran, I have to go.

807
00:51:40,454 --> 00:51:41,497
- No...
- I must do something.

808
00:51:41,497 --> 00:51:43,782
Then let me go with you.

809
00:51:44,542 --> 00:51:47,420
- Together?
- It's better than going alone.

810
00:51:47,420 --> 00:51:49,204
Let me come with you.

811
00:52:00,266 --> 00:52:01,967
Beom Ryong.

812
00:52:06,564 --> 00:52:08,265
Beom Ryong!

813
00:52:10,592 --> 00:52:12,278
Oh.

814
00:52:12,278 --> 00:52:15,781
Sorry, I just need a moment to think.

815
00:52:15,781 --> 00:52:19,285
Oh dear, even if yesterday's visit
didn't go well,

816
00:52:19,285 --> 00:52:21,370
you can't let it affect work like this.

817
00:52:21,370 --> 00:52:22,872
How did you know that, Mr. Cho?

818
00:52:22,872 --> 00:52:24,331
You didn't look like
you were going to headquarters,

819
00:52:24,331 --> 00:52:26,542
so I checked a bit.

820
00:52:26,542 --> 00:52:28,836
What, seeing Chairman Hwang

821
00:52:28,836 --> 00:52:31,589
made you uneasy about teaming up

822
00:52:31,589 --> 00:52:33,257
with a former enemy intelligence agent?

823
00:52:33,257 --> 00:52:34,508
Oh, dear.

824
00:52:34,508 --> 00:52:36,677
I couldn't even bring it up.

825
00:52:36,677 --> 00:52:40,431
My boss thinks I'm teamed up
with Prosecutor Kang.

826
00:52:40,431 --> 00:52:43,592
Oh, it's just...

827
00:52:44,727 --> 00:52:47,938
Well, if Chairman Hwang
already considers us enemies,

828
00:52:47,938 --> 00:52:50,858
no wonder you're not willing
to tell the truth.

829
00:52:50,858 --> 00:52:53,611
But you could just say we are comrades

830
00:52:53,611 --> 00:52:55,562
who took down Yoo In Goo together.

831
00:52:56,489 --> 00:52:59,450
I honestly don't know how to explain it.

832
00:52:59,450 --> 00:53:04,413
Honestly, isn't it true that Jeong Ho Myung
and I could turn on each other at any moment?

833
00:53:04,413 --> 00:53:06,040
What nonsense? Don't be so dramatic.

834
00:53:06,040 --> 00:53:08,334
Ho Myung just talks tough, that's all.

835
00:53:08,334 --> 00:53:10,002
What nonsense are you talking about?

836
00:53:10,002 --> 00:53:12,797
Seriously, you really don't get it.

837
00:53:12,797 --> 00:53:16,833
Do you even know Ho Myung is actually
being considerate of you, Beom Ryong?

838
00:53:18,385 --> 00:53:21,806
- Considerate?
- Ah, well...

839
00:53:21,806 --> 00:53:25,258
I was told not to say this,
but I guess I have to.

840
00:53:34,068 --> 00:53:36,028
Even with a new boss,

841
00:53:36,028 --> 00:53:38,447
our work never changes.

842
00:53:38,447 --> 00:53:42,567
Always surveillance, beatings, threats.

843
00:53:43,744 --> 00:53:45,746
I'm sick of it.

844
00:53:45,746 --> 00:53:47,540
Exactly.

845
00:53:47,540 --> 00:53:49,917
Our boss even got promoted.

846
00:53:49,917 --> 00:53:51,910
Tell me about it.

847
00:54:07,768 --> 00:54:10,053
Over here! Hurry!

848
00:54:17,361 --> 00:54:19,062
What?

849
00:54:20,197 --> 00:54:22,533
- Hello?
- Boss, Kim Seon Jung's wife has shown up.

850
00:54:22,533 --> 00:54:25,703
- What?
- But she came with another woman.

851
00:54:25,703 --> 00:54:29,039
The woman who came in a van
to Kim Seon Jung's house last time.

852
00:54:29,039 --> 00:54:30,124
Oh, right.

853
00:54:30,124 --> 00:54:31,876
The frying pan lady!

854
00:54:31,876 --> 00:54:34,369
- Oh, I remember her.
- What should we do?

855
00:54:35,254 --> 00:54:37,047
Just wait for now.

856
00:54:37,047 --> 00:54:41,010
It's broad daylight,
plenty of witnesses, so hold on.

857
00:54:41,010 --> 00:54:45,880
Stay put. We need men for cleanup.

858
00:55:11,957 --> 00:55:13,667
Yes, boss.

859
00:55:13,667 --> 00:55:17,254
Sergeant Kim, if you're free,
want to go on patrol?

860
00:55:17,254 --> 00:55:20,549
A patrol? You mean now?

861
00:55:20,549 --> 00:55:24,428
Yeah, smooth and clean like usual.

862
00:55:24,428 --> 00:55:26,263
- You know?
- Like usual, fast and clean.

863
00:55:26,263 --> 00:55:28,098
Yes, send me the address.

864
00:55:28,098 --> 00:55:29,966
Yes, boss.

865
00:55:42,696 --> 00:55:44,397
That startled me!

866
00:55:46,848 --> 00:55:48,320
Darn you.

867
00:55:51,705 --> 00:55:55,668
- What brings you here?
- What brings me here? Get off!

868
00:55:55,668 --> 00:55:58,420
- Huh?
- You go back and watch the CCTV.

869
00:55:58,420 --> 00:56:00,455
I'll handle things here.

870
00:56:21,276 --> 00:56:23,737
I heard everything from Mr. Cho.

871
00:56:23,737 --> 00:56:25,522
Mi Kyeong...

872
00:56:26,907 --> 00:56:29,493
was the woman from that van, right?

873
00:56:29,493 --> 00:56:31,078
It's not confirmed yet.

874
00:56:31,078 --> 00:56:33,238
Not confirmed?

875
00:56:34,289 --> 00:56:36,458
But you said you saw her face clearly
at Yeongseon Port.

876
00:56:36,458 --> 00:56:41,213
Since when do you leave me out
just to be considerate?

877
00:56:41,213 --> 00:56:44,290
Do I look like an idiot
who'd lose it over something like this?

878
00:56:45,134 --> 00:56:46,844
Yeah, actually you do.

879
00:56:46,844 --> 00:56:48,795
You little...

880
00:56:52,182 --> 00:56:54,184
Actually, it wasn't for your sake.

881
00:56:54,184 --> 00:56:55,811
We need to stay calm, set aside emotions,

882
00:56:55,811 --> 00:56:57,896
and figure things out properly.

883
00:56:57,896 --> 00:56:59,889
So no need to thank me.

884
00:57:03,318 --> 00:57:05,863
From now on, tell me everything.

885
00:57:05,863 --> 00:57:09,274
We're supposed to be temporary allies,
so there should be no secrets between us!

886
00:57:11,493 --> 00:57:13,361
Answer me.

887
00:57:19,334 --> 00:57:20,753
Is it already patrol time?

888
00:57:20,753 --> 00:57:23,079
We'll know if we follow them.

889
00:57:30,262 --> 00:57:36,301
So... what did you want to talk to me about?

890
00:57:39,688 --> 00:57:41,648
I've thought about this a lot too.

891
00:57:41,648 --> 00:57:43,484
Whether I should even say it...

892
00:57:43,484 --> 00:57:44,902
I mean, from your perspective,

893
00:57:44,902 --> 00:57:47,437
this could be a really serious matter.

894
00:57:48,197 --> 00:57:50,523
But I think you need to know.

895
00:57:51,325 --> 00:57:54,078
Yes, that's right.

896
00:57:54,078 --> 00:57:56,955
If it's difficult, you can tell me later.

897
00:57:56,955 --> 00:57:59,365
But putting it off isn't like me.

898
00:58:00,667 --> 00:58:02,669
- Mr. Bong Jae Soon...
- Just a moment, please.

899
00:58:02,669 --> 00:58:06,298
I mean, it's my first time.
Not exactly first time, but still,

900
00:58:06,298 --> 00:58:08,801
I need some time to think it through.

901
00:58:08,801 --> 00:58:11,970
Right now, it feels very sudden.

902
00:58:11,970 --> 00:58:13,722
Still, you did say you'd accept

903
00:58:13,722 --> 00:58:17,267
whatever your lost past
turns out to be, right?

904
00:58:17,267 --> 00:58:18,968
Pardon?

905
00:58:19,853 --> 00:58:22,764
Oh, yes... I did. But why?

906
00:58:24,399 --> 00:58:26,559
Based on various pieces of evidence,

907
00:58:27,611 --> 00:58:29,655
it's likely you were once

908
00:58:29,655 --> 00:58:32,899
a North Korean special operative,
Mr. Bong Jae Soon.

909
00:58:33,867 --> 00:58:35,568
What?

910
00:58:39,665 --> 00:58:41,574
[North Korean and NIS operatives missing]
Here, read this article.

911
00:58:42,292 --> 00:58:44,294
It says an NIS agent
and a North Korean operative

912
00:58:44,294 --> 00:58:47,005
went missing while making contact on a ferry.

913
00:58:47,005 --> 00:58:50,259
[October 8, 2016]
And look at the article date.

914
00:58:50,259 --> 00:58:53,929
It matches when you were rescued at sea.

915
00:58:53,929 --> 00:58:55,964
And most importantly,

916
00:58:57,724 --> 00:59:00,144
the dress the woman in the photo is wearing,

917
00:59:00,144 --> 00:59:02,396
doesn't it look familiar?

918
00:59:02,396 --> 00:59:07,151
It's the same dress
you showed me yesterday, Jae Soon.

919
00:59:07,151 --> 00:59:08,852
That's ridiculous.

920
00:59:09,736 --> 00:59:12,656
No... Me? A spy?

921
00:59:12,656 --> 00:59:15,576
That's nonsense. Even if I were NIS...

922
00:59:15,576 --> 00:59:17,035
I don't even speak
with a North Korean accent.

923
00:59:17,035 --> 00:59:19,955
And my ID says Bong Jae Soon.
This makes no sense.

924
00:59:19,955 --> 00:59:23,375
Long-term infiltrated agents
often don't use dialects.

925
00:59:23,375 --> 00:59:26,170
And if you were an NIS agent,

926
00:59:26,170 --> 00:59:29,214
they would've contacted you
after the identity check.

927
00:59:29,214 --> 00:59:31,425
But despite all the background checks,

928
00:59:31,425 --> 00:59:35,169
not a single relative or acquaintance
was ever found, right?

929
00:59:36,013 --> 00:59:41,685
All of these circumstances
point very clearly to one conclusion.

930
00:59:41,685 --> 00:59:45,138
It's certain.
You're a North Korean operative.

931
00:59:46,857 --> 00:59:49,392
So I was alone from the start.

932
00:59:50,485 --> 00:59:53,187
I don't have a real family, do I?

933
00:59:54,031 --> 00:59:56,325
Mr. Bong Jae Soon, I know you're confused.

934
00:59:56,325 --> 01:00:01,288
No, I'm just Bong Jae Soon.

935
01:00:01,288 --> 01:00:02,989
Jae Soon!

936
01:00:09,546 --> 01:00:10,547
They're here. Get ready.

937
01:00:10,547 --> 01:00:11,798
- Yes.
- Okay.

938
01:00:11,798 --> 01:00:13,499
Let's go.

939
01:00:23,185 --> 01:00:25,520
Aren't those guys from Heaven Capital?

940
01:00:25,520 --> 01:00:26,688
Yeah.

941
01:00:26,688 --> 01:00:28,315
Shouldn't we step in?

942
01:00:28,315 --> 01:00:31,851
They look like
they're about to start something big.

943
01:00:33,612 --> 01:00:35,197
Huh? Wait, wait, wait!

944
01:00:35,197 --> 01:00:37,199
What are you doing now?

945
01:00:37,199 --> 01:00:39,284
So we're just gonna sit here and watch?

946
01:00:39,284 --> 01:00:40,911
Did you forget Prosecutor Kang's orders?

947
01:00:40,911 --> 01:00:42,746
We're supposed to just monitor the situation.

948
01:00:42,746 --> 01:00:44,957
Don't get involved
and blow things up unnecessarily.

949
01:00:44,957 --> 01:00:48,502
Let's just wait around and handle cleanup

950
01:00:48,502 --> 01:00:50,536
if any report comes in.

951
01:00:52,589 --> 01:00:55,458
I'll go check it out. You stay here.

952
01:00:56,760 --> 01:00:59,763
You think you can handle it alone?
I should go with you.

953
01:00:59,763 --> 01:01:03,675
They know your face. Wait up.

954
01:01:07,437 --> 01:01:09,138
Come on...

955
01:01:23,412 --> 01:01:26,290
Samil-ro 29,
report of a missing 6-year-old child.

956
01:01:26,290 --> 01:01:28,408
We're nearby.

957
01:01:29,209 --> 01:01:30,910
What should we do?

958
01:01:32,337 --> 01:01:35,456
There's nothing much around here.

959
01:01:39,761 --> 01:01:42,306
- Let's head out.
- Okay, okay, sure.

960
01:01:42,306 --> 01:01:44,007
Let's go, let's go.

961
01:01:51,606 --> 01:01:54,276
Please leave. I have nothing to say.

962
01:01:54,276 --> 01:02:00,032
Mr. Park, if something's wrong,
it needs to be corrected.

963
01:02:00,032 --> 01:02:03,785
Didn't you see my husband resigned
because of you?

964
01:02:03,785 --> 01:02:05,454
Stop this.

965
01:02:05,454 --> 01:02:08,582
If you keep doing this,
I'll be the one who gets hurt.

966
01:02:08,582 --> 01:02:10,250
Hurt? What do you mean?

967
01:02:10,250 --> 01:02:13,453
Are you being threatened?

968
01:02:16,798 --> 01:02:19,751
You... who are you people?

969
01:02:20,552 --> 01:02:21,970
What are you waiting for?
Get them out quickly.

970
01:02:21,970 --> 01:02:23,513
What's taking so long? Get them out now!

971
01:02:23,513 --> 01:02:24,723
No, wait...

972
01:02:24,723 --> 01:02:25,891
- No, no.
- Who are you?

973
01:02:25,891 --> 01:02:27,309
Why are you doing this?

974
01:02:27,309 --> 01:02:29,353
- Let go!
- Let's go. Why is she so strong...

975
01:02:29,353 --> 01:02:30,354
- No...
- What's wrong?

976
01:02:30,354 --> 01:02:32,439
It doesn't have to go this far!

977
01:02:32,439 --> 01:02:34,149
Oh, no!

978
01:02:34,149 --> 01:02:35,359
Let go right now!

979
01:02:35,359 --> 01:02:37,152
What are you doing? Can't handle her alone?

980
01:02:37,152 --> 01:02:39,321
Come out!

981
01:02:39,321 --> 01:02:41,031
Please save me! Please...

982
01:02:41,031 --> 01:02:44,034
Chang Soo, if you help me this once,
I can turn things around.

983
01:02:44,034 --> 01:02:46,578
Word spreads fast in this world.

984
01:02:46,578 --> 01:02:48,955
You lost the drugs and ended up broke,

985
01:02:48,955 --> 01:02:50,665
and your backing's all gone.

986
01:02:50,665 --> 01:02:51,917
So what makes you think I'd help you?

987
01:02:51,917 --> 01:02:53,696
You traitor! You can't do this to me.

988
01:02:53,696 --> 01:02:57,714
A guy who stabbed his boss

989
01:02:57,714 --> 01:02:59,216
is talking about loyalty?

990
01:02:59,216 --> 01:03:00,717
Don't splash your mess on me.

991
01:03:00,717 --> 01:03:02,386
Keep your head down and stay quiet.

992
01:03:02,386 --> 01:03:03,970
What?

993
01:03:03,970 --> 01:03:05,797
Darn it!

994
01:03:19,069 --> 01:03:21,071
Martial arts master.

995
01:03:21,071 --> 01:03:22,239
Prosecutor Kang Young Ae?

996
01:03:22,239 --> 01:03:24,190
Why are those two still alive?

997
01:03:27,661 --> 01:03:29,904
Those two have been colluding the whole time?

998
01:03:32,541 --> 01:03:34,709
If I'm going down,

999
01:03:34,709 --> 01:03:37,620
I'm taking all of you with me!

1000
01:04:00,026 --> 01:04:01,727
Jae Soon!

1001
01:04:07,576 --> 01:04:11,104
- Let go!
- Just let us go!

1002
01:04:18,336 --> 01:04:20,037
Stop this!

1003
01:04:23,175 --> 01:04:24,342
Is this woman insane?

1004
01:04:24,342 --> 01:04:25,969
- Come out.
- Let go!

1005
01:04:25,969 --> 01:04:27,012
- Move!
- Let go!

1006
01:04:27,012 --> 01:04:29,422
Have you lost your mind?

1007
01:04:44,404 --> 01:04:46,912
Huh? A knife!

1008
01:05:23,264 --> 01:05:24,418
Have you really made up your mind?

1009
01:05:24,418 --> 01:05:25,568
I'm going to tell her everything.

1010
01:05:25,568 --> 01:05:27,812
I was a black ops agent from the NIS.

1011
01:05:27,812 --> 01:05:29,917
You've been deceiving me for ten years.

1012
01:05:29,917 --> 01:05:32,431
Those guys are truly horrible.

1013
01:05:32,431 --> 01:05:34,944
They're not opponents
that an ordinary officer can take on.

1014
01:05:34,944 --> 01:05:37,408
I don't see any reason
I should listen to you.

1015
01:05:37,408 --> 01:05:39,008
What do you think of my uncle?

1016
01:05:39,008 --> 01:05:40,647
He seems like a really good person.

1017
01:05:40,647 --> 01:05:42,464
Bulgae is not amnesiac.

1018
01:05:42,464 --> 01:05:44,530
Bulgae, a human weapon
trained in North Korea.

1019
01:05:44,530 --> 01:05:46,144
I really don't remember.

1020
01:05:46,144 --> 01:05:47,456
There's definitely some scheme behind this.

1021
01:05:47,456 --> 01:05:49,696
From what I see, it looks like
he really lost all his memory.

1022
01:05:49,696 --> 01:05:51,168
Don't get any ideas, you darn spy.

1023
01:05:51,168 --> 01:05:54,272
He's not Bong Jae Soon, but Bulgae.

